Yesterday I was playing a character which had a ring of regeneration, and doing
the usual shuffling in and out as my HP status changed. At some point I entered
a room full of killer bees, and typed PU instead of Pu. No big deal, 'u' wasn't
anything you can put on, but I didn't notice under I saw the bottom line shift
one character to the left and saw I had 8hp left. At this point I put the ring
on and didn't get killed, but this made me think about the whole business and
wonder whether there ought to be a way for me to save myself all these
keystrokes and avoid making such mistakes (yes, I know, it was an error and it
was my fault, but I had to do this Pu/Ru business so often that I no longer
paid attention to it).

Well, I thought about having a kind of automatic mode for the ring whereby the
computer would assume that the player is keying Rx when he no longer needs the
ring, and vice-versa (the ring could be triggered in and out of this mode with
an 'ax' (apply) command), but realized the implications on potentially wasted
turns at the wrong moment and decided this wasn't a good idea (it would have to
do this only when you are not in danger, and this isn't something easy to
define unfortunately). But perhaps a much simpler solution is to have blessed
rings of regeneration cause hunger only when they actually do something? This
would still use up one finger (and probably one potion of holy water as well)
but would make life much more comfortable... Comments?

  Eric


